                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "spør",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": " when the meaning is asks whether. Say "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "Hun spør om du kommer",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "imported_section_003",
      "role": "contrast",
      "objective_ids": [
        "obj_condition_hvis"
      ],
      "title": "Choosing by meaning",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The choice is not about the English word. It is about the job of the clause. Ask: is it a condition, or is it an embedded yes/no question?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "col_langs": [
            "en",
            "no",
            "no"
          ],
          "headers": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Meaning"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Use"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Example"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Condition"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "hvis"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Jeg går hvis du går."
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Embedded yes/no question"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "om"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Jeg spør om du går."
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Formal or written conditional alternative"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "om"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Om du ønsker det, kan vi endre planen."
                }
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Om",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " can sometimes introduce a condition, especially in more formal or written Norwegian. For everyday learner Norwegian, "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " is the clear default for conditions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Om du vil, kan vi ta en pause."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If you want, we can take a break."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Because both words can sometimes translate as if, the strongest habit is to translate the meaning first: condition goes to "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "; whether-question goes to "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "om",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
